Fukakusa OCR — licence statement

1. Model weights, label maps and derived tables (the vit-v2 and vit-v1 model.safetensors and config.json files, the label files labels-jibo-v2.tar.gz,
   labels/*.json, labels/variants.csv, labels/class_prior.json): Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. They are derived from the CODH Kuzushiji dataset
   (人文学オープンデータ共同利用センター / 国文学研究資料館, http://codh.rois.ac.jp/char-shape/, CC BY-SA 4.0), whose attribution
   terms carry over. When you redistribute or adapt them, credit "Center for Open Data in the Humanities (CODH), Kuzushiji
   dataset" and "Atkins, Chau and Zeng, Fukakusa (University of Washington)".
2. Detector weights (yolo11m-kuzu-v6.pt): fine-tuned from Ultralytics YOLO11m, which is released under AGPL-3.0; the fine-tuned
   weights are distributed under AGPL-3.0 as well, https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html. Use the classifier alone if the
   AGPL terms do not suit your project.
2b. Cascade R-CNN weights (rcnn-res101-5-10.pth, mmdetection 3.3.0 checkpoint): CC BY-SA 4.0 as under item 1; the mmdetection code it
   requires is Apache-2.0.
3. Example images under examples/ and fixtures/crops/: pages of the CODH Kuzushiji dataset, CC BY-SA 4.0, with the manuscript identifier and the
   CODH page URL recorded in examples/README.md.
4. Source code in fukakusa_ocr/, training/, evaluation/ and scripts/: Copyright (c) 2025–2026 Paul S. Atkins, Herman Chau, Michael R. Zeng. Released under the
   same CC BY-SA 4.0 terms as the weights so that the package can be redistributed as one unit. The authors may re-license the
   code at a later date; this statement applies to this release.
